//! A runtime error raised before a negation is reached, in a tick where the negation flips to false. The negation
//! reads the `let`'s output, so it runs after the division (LANGUAGE §9.14).
program error_before_a_flipping_negation version 1;
input ia(x: u8);
input ib(x: u8);
view out(x, y) = ia(x), let y = 10 / x, not ib(y);
